    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0761" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/590</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Military Attaché in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barrett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the War Department
                    </hi><anchor n="69" xml:id="d729-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-13">August 13,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>New military air field built by Chinese 30 miles up river. Two hundred
                    twenty-five Soviet planes recently arrived China and less than that number
                    Soviet pilots according to reliable source who states also that 60 pursuits to
                    be allotted defense of Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d729-f1" n="69" type="source" xml:id="d729-f1-content">
                <p>Paraphrase of radiogram received at the War Department, August 13, 9:54 p.m., and
                    transmitted to the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
